// Shotgun fire effects. The holes, the impact puffs and the muzzle burst are client
// frame commands on the weapon's "fire" animation (weapon_shotgun.tik); the grenade's
// explosion is the fx_grenade_explosion.tik event entity.
// For the real client (capture.ps1 runs it on both games): turn a
// little right and aim a little down, so the blast lands beside Julie rather than
// behind her, fire the primary and take screenshots of the burst, the puffs and the
// holes; then fire the alternate (grenade) and catch its explosion.
// A dual-handed weapon's primary is +attackleft, its alternate +attackright
// (julie_torso.st, CHECK_ATTACK_LEFT / CHECK_ATTACK_RIGHT).
probe:
waitforplayer
wait 2
stuffcmd "give weapon_shotgun.tik"
wait 0.5
stuffcmd "use Shotgun dual"
wait 2
stuffcmd "+right"
wait 0.2
stuffcmd "-right"
stuffcmd "+lookdown"
wait 0.25
stuffcmd "-lookdown"
wait 0.3
stuffcmd "+attackleft"
wait 0.1
stuffcmd "-attackleft"
wait 0.1
stuffcmd "screenshot"
wait 0.6
stuffcmd "screenshot"
wait 1.5
stuffcmd "screenshot"
wait 1
stuffcmd "+attackright"
wait 0.1
stuffcmd "-attackright"
wait 2.15
stuffcmd "screenshot"
wait 1.5
stuffcmd "screenshot"
wait 0.5
stuffcmd "whatis 0"
stuffcmd "levelvars"
stuffcmd "pendingevents"
stuffcmd "quit"
end
